it's not often that I tell people to  simply not buy a new device that I'm  reviewing companies typically improve  their tack year-to-year or make  something new that tries to stand out in  the market but not this time the Galaxy  Tab s6 is samsung latest tablet but when  I started to use it and test it I kept  finding things about it that are worse  than last year's model I'll go over  every corner that was cut in just a bit  but first I just want to say that there  are two alternative tablets listed down  in the description that are much better  buys both Android and iPad OS the tab s6  lights biggest selling point is the  price coming in at just $350 so $50 less  than last year's s5e with that $50 price  drop it has gained two features that the  s5 II didn't have and that is s-pen  support and a headphone jack the biggest  competitors to the s5 II  Apple's budget iPad has both of those I  can see why samsung added them  unfortunately in order to have those  features and also meet a competitive  price point and ended up killing this  device for me personally and the one  group of people that this would have  actually been perfect for should just go  and buy last year's s5e let's start with  the display I love the s5 ease sharp  olla display which was fantastic for  watching video with its deep blacks and  for reading with it's over 4 million  pixels but now it is a dull TFT display  which is 2.4 million pixels and the  difference is definitely noticeable  because of that change  it is almost 30% thicker and 15% heavier  now it's still usable as a tablet it's  just not as good on the sides we have  dual speakers which are actually fairly  loud and sound good but still not as  good as the s5 ease quad speakers  probably the most frustrating change is  the removal of the keyboard dock  connector I love that we can attach  keyboards to these newer tablets and use  many of them for serious typing and the  s5 es worked fairly well for that so it  makes no sense to me why Samsung got rid  of it my only guess is that they didn't  want to invest the money to make a new  keyboard so now you will have to just  use a third party Bluetooth keyboard  that won't be as good now let's talk  about the pen support that they gave us  when they took away the keyboard  benefit is that the S Pen is now  included in the box but it's super  lightweight and kind of cheap feeling  when we draw on the screen there is a  massive delay probably the worst that  I've experienced it seems to be a mix of  screen delay and the graphics not  keeping up because they did leave Aries  almost like frames are being sometimes  dropped and this is just what simple  drawing not something that's complex  like a project with multiple layers  overall the pen experience is quite poor  it's worse than the budget surface go to  and much worse than a basic iPad that  cost 329 but most of the time comes in  well under that we'll have some links in  the description because of it lag in the  fact that iOS has so many great apps  with pen supports if you're thinking  about buying in the s6 light just for  the pen I always strongly suggest going  and picking up one of these basic iPads  instead let me quickly cover cameras  last year we had 13 megapixels on the  rear and eight on the front but a year  later they got worse we had eight  megapixels on the back and five on the  front now on top of that we no longer  have the ultra-fast fingerprint scanner  on the side and now we're going back to  the days of just punching in your PIN or  using basic facial recognition which is  kind of unreliable and can be fooled  with pictures now for the one true  complaint that I had with the s5e last  year the processor we had the budget  snapdragon 670 which was quite slow and  made the tablet sluggish so when I saw  that Samsung got rid of it this year I  was happy well until I tested it this  year samsung is using their own 8-quart  Exynos 96 11 but when I tested it I  found that it is actually slower than  already slow 670 and keep in mind it's  been a year so the biggest issue wasn't  improved now graphics did get slightly  faster but not enough to make a  difference in the real world and the  worst part of all is that this chip is  less efficient so the battery life  rating has gone down by three hours  battery itself is the same but that  included charger is now a 7.5 watt slow  charger instead of that 18 watt fast  charger so we'll take more than twice as  long to charge and the battery lasts  about 25%  yes I am being very critical of this  tablet where many other reviewers are  being much nicer almost too nice and not  even mentioning what has gone down in  quality and yes you can still use this  buy it use it as a regular tablet and  they will do okay you'll have a decent  experience with simple apps and maybe  basic games web browsing maybe watching  some movies but that doesn't mean that  you should buy it  Samson went from an overall fantastic  tablet that had a few shortcomings to  one that is overall the complete  opposite as a few good things going for  it but if you don't need the pen support  and don't mind using a USB type-c  adapter or a Bluetooth earbuds just go  buy the s5 II instead or you can spend a  little bit more money and check out  their really good standard tab s6 I'll  go ahead and leave some links in the  description and you guys can watch the  tab s6 review right over there thank you  guys for watching let me know your  thoughts down in the comment section  below click above to subscribe this man  max max tech and I will see you in the  next video  [Music]
 

